    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d907">

                <pb facs="0982" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg696"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3034</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-01T13:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 1, 1916, 1 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8.45 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>294. Understand that Swedish Government has approached neutral powers, including
                    United States, with a view to securing joint action on questions affecting them.
                    Am informed confidentially by French Embassy that Spanish reply amounts
                    practically to statement that Spain would take only such action as England and
                    France desired. French and British Embassies consider Swedish proposals, which
                    are apparently strongly seconded by Switzerland, as clearly directed against
                    Allies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
